                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "19fafe6e-5618-371f-9c61-849c6730ce57",
                        "entry_id": "ea3981c9-fb17-31ed-9ee6-e747ba676f18",
                        "glosses": [
                            "разжёвывать как следует, до конца, полностью перетирать, измельчать, жуя"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "aef940c8-009b-4109-8ae9-f000071de398",
                                "sense_id": "19fafe6e-5618-371f-9c61-849c6730ce57",
                                "text": "Буфетчик из вежливости положил кусочек в рот и сразу понял, что жуёт что-то действительно очень свежее и, главное, необыкновенно вкусное. Но, прожёвывая душистое, сочное мясо, буфетчик едва не подавился и не упал вторично."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5c919cdf-7c51-4f7b-a0f5-15f508c4e61b",
                        "source_entry_id": "ea3981c9-fb17-31ed-9ee6-e747ba676f18",
                        "source_sense_id": "19fafe6e-5618-371f-9c61-849c6730ce57",
                        "target_lang_word": "chew",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "chew",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "051a8c90-0a5f-3c8c-9e24-8ad68b5b06d2",
                                        "entry_id": "f9395c01-72c0-3041-9ab5-e9cebf2c8f20",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To crush with the teeth by repeated closing and opening of the jaws; done to food to soften it and break it down by the action of saliva before it is swallowed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a16ee955-13ba-427d-b361-bac0f9bc3564",
                                                "sense_id": "051a8c90-0a5f-3c8c-9e24-8ad68b5b06d2",
                                                "text": "Make sure to chew thoroughly, and don't talk with your mouth full!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0cc9cbf9-e7a8-493e-8e5e-3564352c34bd",
                                                "sense_id": "051a8c90-0a5f-3c8c-9e24-8ad68b5b06d2",
                                                "text": "The steak was tough to chew as it had been cooked too long."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4d9afe76-b2e4-42b9-8c12-67fae141a457",
                                                "sense_id": "051a8c90-0a5f-3c8c-9e24-8ad68b5b06d2",
                                                "text": "The same chewn upon maketh one to avoid much phlegm."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fa9c6edc-2e72-4b51-9d50-83d99060f5b9",
                                                "sense_id": "051a8c90-0a5f-3c8c-9e24-8ad68b5b06d2",
                                                "text": "1971-79, Journal of Glenn T. Seaborg\nAnd gruesome they areː We find cattle still alive with hindquarters chewn off, still alive with their eyes chewn out, their ears chewn off, their noses and faces chewn till they look like (a) Hamburger, their tails hanging in shreds. Or, we find them after a slow and cruel death. Can you understand why cattlemen will shoot YOUR dog if he is seen wandering on ranchland?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe8d689b-06fa-4293-8a26-c39fca354ed6",
                                                "sense_id": "051a8c90-0a5f-3c8c-9e24-8ad68b5b06d2",
                                                "text": "But meanwhile Mademoiselle's book had at least been found under an arm-chair where it had been dragged, chewn up and torn to pieces by a young pug-dog or by a kitten."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "501b718c-b51f-4242-b96d-ad266097f925",
                                                "sense_id": "051a8c90-0a5f-3c8c-9e24-8ad68b5b06d2",
                                                "text": "He wore two sweaters, both moth chewn and filthy but warm."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2f858586-3bd1-4845-94b5-f38ae2ea0848",
                                                "sense_id": "051a8c90-0a5f-3c8c-9e24-8ad68b5b06d2",
                                                "text": "His left cheek seemed to have been cut and chewn awayǃ"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3b8ab024-8992-3383-8539-0cde29da8d6a",
                                        "entry_id": "f9395c01-72c0-3041-9ab5-e9cebf2c8f20",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To grind, tear, or otherwise degrade or demolish something with teeth or as with teeth."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "39fe55d2-cc33-4518-be83-7de1fb5bf8f3",
                                                "sense_id": "3b8ab024-8992-3383-8539-0cde29da8d6a",
                                                "text": "He keeps his feed in steel drums to prevent the mice from chewing holes in the feed-sacks."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "edd1f6e6-013d-4833-8817-7d28412ca484",
                                                "sense_id": "3b8ab024-8992-3383-8539-0cde29da8d6a",
                                                "text": "The harsh desert wind and sand had chewed the stump into ragged strips of wood."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7730cd50-972b-3da1-a905-9cbb06b5930f",
                                        "entry_id": "f9395c01-72c0-3041-9ab5-e9cebf2c8f20",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To think about something; to ponder; to chew over."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "164905e5-f6a1-44c3-8858-2a4ce524af03",
                                                "sense_id": "7730cd50-972b-3da1-a905-9cbb06b5930f",
                                                "text": "The professor stood at the blackboard, chalk in hand, and chewed the question the student had asked."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5a517504-4b26-42aa-b084-3fbff5ab08fc",
                                                "sense_id": "7730cd50-972b-3da1-a905-9cbb06b5930f",
                                                "text": "Old politicians chew on wisdom past."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b0813094-0ac0-4e61-b027-de47b1a51e02",
                                                "sense_id": "7730cd50-972b-3da1-a905-9cbb06b5930f",
                                                "text": "He chews revenge, abjuring his offense."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "chew",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5a502f3d-cab1-3afb-88eb-7aa1faa2e5c6",
                                        "entry_id": "b26e9e2a-c2fc-3960-b2d0-bdfb629a6f95",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of chewing; mastication with the mouth."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7d921625-41ed-4b98-a05f-6fcaf719f830",
                                                "sense_id": "5a502f3d-cab1-3afb-88eb-7aa1faa2e5c6",
                                                "text": "I popped the gum into my mouth and gave it a chew."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "afb8b981-2df8-3313-8b34-63d90acd042e",
                                        "entry_id": "b26e9e2a-c2fc-3960-b2d0-bdfb629a6f95",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Level of chewiness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd9323de-c953-4de2-840d-f32d72c9ba1a",
                                                "sense_id": "afb8b981-2df8-3313-8b34-63d90acd042e",
                                                "text": "Once it's cooked, it's not enough of a hard chew to count."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2e5bcbe5-26ac-4867-a45e-3db40588aae0",
                                                "sense_id": "afb8b981-2df8-3313-8b34-63d90acd042e",
                                                "text": "A bread with a strong and solidified gluten network has a nice chew to it, and many types of charcuterie call for just enough work by the teeth to be dangerously addictive. But in all cases, chewy must be combined with an appropriate amount of ..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "62aba8fd-ce1b-42b6-aec6-1d330e3a8385",
                                                "sense_id": "afb8b981-2df8-3313-8b34-63d90acd042e",
                                                "text": "No matter what I did to the squid, it was a tough chew. I got out my magnifying glass. Still, there was nothing that I could see to make the squid curl when cooked. I decided to tenderize the squid with my rubber hammer."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f23aac04-6730-429c-8862-a20e0199f528",
                                                "sense_id": "afb8b981-2df8-3313-8b34-63d90acd042e",
                                                "text": "To serve, cook the malloredus in a large pot of boiling salted water until just tender, but with a nice chew to them. Fold into a warm sauce or ragout and serve immediately."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c2ce1f8f-ac07-4f7b-93fa-d728acae612e",
                                                "sense_id": "afb8b981-2df8-3313-8b34-63d90acd042e",
                                                "text": "While these are a little complicated to make, the result is a thick, toothsome bun that has a nice chew to it but is still soft."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bfe4f37d-2b32-3db9-8443-f887ae79ed3f",
                                        "entry_id": "b26e9e2a-c2fc-3960-b2d0-bdfb629a6f95",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A small sweet, such as a taffy, that is eaten by chewing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3d8c9a12-4352-49a9-a034-23d7d2de5627",
                                                "sense_id": "bfe4f37d-2b32-3db9-8443-f887ae79ed3f",
                                                "text": "Phillip purchased a bag of licorice chews at the drugstore."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "377315e8-fa3f-34f3-ab83-a54ddb4c82a5",
                                        "entry_id": "b26e9e2a-c2fc-3960-b2d0-bdfb629a6f95",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Chewing tobacco."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ce213d33-77f0-46d6-afe3-eec64043b49e",
                                                "sense_id": "377315e8-fa3f-34f3-ab83-a54ddb4c82a5",
                                                "text": "The school had banned chew and smokes from the school grounds, even for adults."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fe70783e-4c43-313a-b819-af681cad93c8",
                                        "entry_id": "b26e9e2a-c2fc-3960-b2d0-bdfb629a6f95",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A plug or wad of chewing tobacco; chaw or a chaw."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "46552ced-0afe-41df-9f46-728b92e25bd2",
                                                "sense_id": "fe70783e-4c43-313a-b819-af681cad93c8",
                                                "text": "The ballplayers sat on the bench watching the rain, glumly working their chews."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "01cc4ef6-e65f-46cd-bde8-720602818769",
                                                "sense_id": "fe70783e-4c43-313a-b819-af681cad93c8",
                                                "text": "The first time he chewed tobacco, he swallowed his chew and got extremely sick."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ae723414-acfc-3e32-8c4e-f3f0cdccf10d",
                                        "entry_id": "b26e9e2a-c2fc-3960-b2d0-bdfb629a6f95",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The condition of something being torn or ground up mechanically."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6682243-71e4-4843-aed1-aa31741949cc",
                                                "sense_id": "ae723414-acfc-3e32-8c4e-f3f0cdccf10d",
                                                "text": "Avoiding Tape Chew. In the early days of the ADAT, the \"V\" blocks (two arms that thread the tape around the front of the head) could sometimes get out of alignment and \"chew\" the outside track […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a775057d-df44-4838-b316-228063b04810",
                        "source_entry_id": "ea3981c9-fb17-31ed-9ee6-e747ba676f18",
                        "source_sense_id": "19fafe6e-5618-371f-9c61-849c6730ce57",
                        "target_lang_word": "masticate",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "masticate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c347f135-e829-38d6-8243-c99266631aa3",
                                        "entry_id": "e0e86fe8-f674-3159-b46c-239517014af0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To chew (usually food)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "36fcd0b3-c9c0-4936-b5f0-ca2ac1d330ec",
                                                "sense_id": "c347f135-e829-38d6-8243-c99266631aa3",
                                                "text": "\"By tasting it, to be sure,\" said I, masticating a morsel that Kory-Kory had just put in my mouth."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a4a7c4e5-3fad-4ca1-8c3d-2ca2e385186a",
                                                "sense_id": "c347f135-e829-38d6-8243-c99266631aa3",
                                                "text": "He resumed his meal. \"I had no idea of it,\" he said, and masticated."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2c316b7d-e919-437e-91b6-4e7e331f3c58",
                                                "sense_id": "c347f135-e829-38d6-8243-c99266631aa3",
                                                "text": "The friends watch the two make their way between other habitués masticating, drinking, crouched in a scrum of conversation[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a2c71b5-5c1f-4823-af90-df36f9ee8615",
                                                "sense_id": "c347f135-e829-38d6-8243-c99266631aa3",
                                                "text": "The vegetables were not to be cooked but merely grated fine, if I could not masticate them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "685acf98-273d-4b91-8655-61ee5d46bf49",
                                                "sense_id": "c347f135-e829-38d6-8243-c99266631aa3",
                                                "text": "The cow stood, quietly masticating its cud."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a0abc2a8-4dec-4041-a2a8-488b9373ae56",
                                                "sense_id": "c347f135-e829-38d6-8243-c99266631aa3",
                                                "text": "The fat boy rose, opened his eyes, swallowed the huge piece of pie he had been in the act of masticating when he last fell asleep, and slowly obeyed his master’s orders."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aba3b01e-b999-4729-a82c-8a55a2a8e5f9",
                                                "sense_id": "c347f135-e829-38d6-8243-c99266631aa3",
                                                "text": "At the moment Carter snapped, a lunch break in J&M turned into a blood riot when half a dozen technicians dropped their snacks and began cannibalizing each other instead. In I&T, their opposite numbers began beating each other to death with keyboards, chairs, and even computer monitors while their Chief masticated her husband's digits."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "583173a4-840e-3ccd-8aca-1e6675973070",
                                        "entry_id": "e0e86fe8-f674-3159-b46c-239517014af0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To grind or knead something into a pulp."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
